From 3186637b2d4f3f3e830b8b011d461a28caea806d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Feb 2026 21:09:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: tegra-hsp: enable per-mailbox EMPTY interrupt on
 send

When has_per_mb_ie is true (Tegra234/264), enable the per-mailbox
HSP_SM_SHRD_MBOX_EMPTY_INT_IE register when sending messages. Without
this, TX completion interrupts never fire and the mailbox queue fills
up with "Try increasing MBOX_TX_QUEUE_LEN" errors.

The per-mailbox EMPTY interrupt enable register is disabled at mailbox
startup for producers, but was never re-enabled when sending data. The
shared interrupt register (HSP_INT_IE) is enabled, but on platforms
with has_per_mb_ie = true, both registers must be enabled for the
interrupt to fire.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
---
 drivers/mailbox/tegra-hsp.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mailbox/tegra-hsp.c b/drivers/mailbox/tegra-hsp.c
index 5d33cf8ec2ec..b6f62f1d6b4b 100644
--- a/drivers/mailbox/tegra-hsp.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/tegra-hsp.c
@@ -479,6 +479,11 @@ static int tegra_hsp_mailbox_send_data(struct mbox_chan *chan, void *data)

 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hsp->lock, flags);

+	/* enable per-mailbox EMPTY interrupt for Tegra234/264 */
+	if (hsp->soc->has_per_mb_ie)
+		tegra_hsp_channel_writel(&mb->channel, 0x1,
+					 HSP_SM_SHRD_MBOX_EMPTY_INT_IE);
+
 	return 0;
 }

